{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_574","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -C 2 'Holdout result|Iteration 8|Iteration 9|Verdict.\\\\*\\\\* Keep the August' agent/journal.md\"","aggregated_output":"128-**Verdict.** Discard the all-week regression under the pre-registered consistency rule. The observed weekend/weekday split motivates a separate, explicitly conditional test below; it is not evidence that the all-week rule works.\n129-\n130:## Iteration 8 — newer calendar fit for COM_EQU (planned)\n131-\n132-**Hypothesis.** SPCX and SP500 had relatively little history in the July 31 calendar fit. Adding the complete August month may reduce hourly-profile noise and lower September COM_EQU_24H CRPS.\n--\n136-**Short-screen result.** On September 9–10, the eight-asset COM_EQU_24H mean CRPS moved from 2402.94 with the July profile to 2396.84 with the August 31 profile (0.25% lower). Seven assets improved; NVDAX regressed by 0.04%, below the stated 1% cutoff. SPCX had the largest gain, 4065.71 → 4029.84 (0.88%). This passes the screen for the nonoverlapping September 1–8 check.\n137-\n138:**Holdout result.** On the nonoverlapping September 1–8 scored dates, all eight COM_EQU assets improved with the August 31 profile. The unweighted mean CRPS fell from 1890.25 to 1881.08 (0.49%). Each asset had 192 exact prompts, 1000 paths, and full realized coverage. The largest relative gains were NVDAX 0.83%, AAPLX 0.73%, and SPCX 0.70%.\n139-\n140:**Verdict.** Keep the August 31 calendar profile for COM_EQU_24H.\n141-\n142:## Iteration 9 — weekend-only hourly regression (planned)\n143-\n144-**Hypothesis.** The HAR variance forecast's August benefit may reflect quieter weekends; applying it only to crypto 1-hour prompts starting on Saturday or Sunday may retain that benefit without its September weekday regression.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
